            <td class={tdClass}>Old telegrams, textbook pages, printed references</td>
            <td class={tdClass}>Very good</td>
            <td class={tdClass}>Flat and evenly lit, though old prints can lose contrast over time</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class={tdClass}>Photos</td>
            <td class={tdClass}>Camera pictures of printed or displayed Morse</td>
            <td class={tdClass}>Good</td>
            <td class={tdClass}>Lighting, angle, and focus can all shift pixel widths, which is what the tool measures</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class={tdClass}>Handwritten Morse</td>
            <td class={tdClass}>Notes with hand-drawn dots and dashes</td>
            <td class={tdClass}>Varies</td>
            <td class={tdClass}>Spacing depends on the person's hand, and that spacing is what tells a dot from a dash</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
